You do remember how we reacted to Japanese culture the last time we had a major war with them right? WWIII and the lead-up didn't see internment camps or anything, or even anything so bad as the Alien and Sedition Acts, but there were import bans and boycotts of Japanese products, and no one was stupid enough to advertise that they liked content made in a country that was now their enemy. How many positive depictions of Russia have you seen in the last few years?